<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sargis I Jaqeli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sargis I Jaqeli was the ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samtskhe">Samtskhe</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> in the second half of the 13th century and founder of the principality's independence. By securing direct recognition from the Mongol <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>, he placed his lands outside the authority of the Georgian kings, and his descendants ruled Samtskhe as hereditary atabegs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sargis-i-jaqeli.jpg" alt="Sargis I Jaqeli" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 14th century CE · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_Sargis_I_Jaqeli.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
